{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>When your son asks you tomorrow.</b> There is a מָחָר that is now, and there is a מָחָר that is after an interval — like this one, and like ״וְלֹא יֹאמְרוּ בְנֵיכֶם מָחָר לְבָנֵינוּ״ (Joshua 22) — that is, the children of Gad and the children of Reuben." "<b>What is this.</b> This is a simple child who does not know how to deepen his question, and asks bluntly, ״What is this?״ And in another place it says ״מָה הָעֵדֹת וְהַחֻקִּים וְהַמִּשְׁפָּטִים וגו׳״ (Deuteronomy 6) — that is the question of a wise son. Scripture spoke of four sons: the wicked, and the one who does not know how to ask, and the one who asks bluntly, and the one who asks wisely (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:57.867332918Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}